<p>I've thought on two more problems for me as well:</p>
<ul>
<li>First off, referring to the quoted passage above, I didn't really receive any indication of urgency from the adults other than them being busy and yelling with each other once. The fact that the girl goes to space and then goes back in a very small part of the article framed this story to seem more like an isolated accident, with a narrow perspective of the actual story (running whatever's in space).</li>
